internetarchive (Python and command-Line interface to Archive.org)

This package installs a command-line tool named ia for using
Archive.org from the command-line. It also installs the
internetarchive Python module for programatic access to archive.org.

It's not obvious from the documentation, but search terms for the
'ia search' command should be quoted if they contain spaces. Also,
an archive.org account is *not* required for read-only access
(e.g. search and download).

Documentation is available at:
https://archive.org/services/docs/api/internetarchive

Note: 5.10.1 is the last version that will run on Slackware 15.0.
Newer versions require a newer Python than 3.9, so this won't be
upgraded until the next Slackware release. Sorry.
